# sms_pairs.conf -- directed communication policy for inter-agent messaging.
# Read by shared/lib/sms.py, fresh at every send. FAIL-CLOSED: a missing,
# unreadable, empty, or malformed file allows nothing, and one malformed
# non-comment line voids the entire policy (a typo must not silently yield
# a partial matrix).
#
# One directed pair per line: sender -> recipient. Each name must match
# [a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,31}; a self-pair voids the policy. sms.py enforces
# syntax and membership ONLY -- it does not check that a name belongs to a
# chartered agent, so a misspelled name yields a pair that simply never
# matches. Charter existence is enforced where it is owned: meet.py refuses
# to convene an agent with no charter file.
#
# install.sh installs this file as /etc/treebeard/sms_pairs.conf if none is
# present. It authorises nothing: until pairs are added every send is
# refused and audited as policy-error, which is the expected first-run
# state, not a fault.
#
# agent_a -> agent_b
# agent_b -> agent_a
